# --help for every subcommand and nested verb (T60.2)

Top-level `rtok --help` stays in `help.toml`. `web` and `tui` are help-only
here: a server and a TTY are not snapshot material.

```console
$ rtok hook --help
Claude Code hook entry point: reads the event JSON on stdin, writes JSON to stdout

Usage: rtok hook [OPTIONS] [EVENT]

Arguments:
  [EVENT]  

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --host <HOST>    Overlay `[hook] host` (`claude` | `cursor` | `copilot` | `devin` | `cline`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok mcp --help
Serve MCP tools over stdio; `-- <server argv>` wraps a foreign server instead

Usage: rtok mcp [OPTIONS] [-- <WRAP>...] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  ping  Prove the agent's rtok MCP server is alive and answering
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [WRAP]...  Foreign stdio MCP server to wrap losslessly (`rtok mcp -- npx some-server`)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --call <TOOL>    Call one listed tool and print the text result (pi `registerTool` shim)
      --json <ARGS>    JSON arguments for `--call`
      --host <HOST>    The host this MCP entry belongs to (`claude`, `cursor`, `grok`, …): overlays
                       `[hook] host` so the process can find its rtok agent
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok proxy --help
Local API proxy for ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL

Usage: rtok proxy [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>        User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --port <PORT>          Override `[proxy] port`
      --upstream <UPSTREAM>  Override `[proxy] upstream`
      --mode <MODE>          Override `[proxy] mode` (`passthrough` | `compress`)
      --dry-run              Print effective `[proxy]` settings and exit
  -h, --help                 Print help

$ rtok web --help
Local web UI over the same data as `rtok tui` (WebSocket API + React SPA)

Usage: rtok web [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --host <HOST>    Override `[web] host`
      --port <PORT>    Override `[web] port`
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok tui --help
Terminal UI over the same data as `rtok web` (one model, two renderings)

Usage: rtok tui [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>          User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --tab <TAB>              Start on this tab (a page name both surfaces carry)
      --tick-secs <TICK_SECS>  Model re-read cadence in seconds
  -h, --help                   Print help

$ rtok stats --help
Measurements from session logs and the proxy

Usage: rtok stats [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>         User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --since <SINCE>         How far back to read transcripts (`60d`, `24h`)
      --json                  JSON instead of the table
      --plugin <PLUGIN>       Restrict to one tool or plugin id
      --save-baseline <NAME>  Write this report JSON to `<home>/measurements/<name>.json`
      --compare <NAME>        Print deltas against a saved baseline
      --calibrate             Fit chars-per-token via count_tokens (skipped without an API key)
      --cache                 Cache health per session from proxy usage rows: busts and their cause
      --price                 Show per-model USD costs from `[stats.prices]` (`--price`)
  -h, --help                  Print help

$ rtok bench --help
A/B benchmark of host configurations

Usage: rtok bench [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>      User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --tasks <TASKS>      Task list TOML
      --runs <RUNS>        Repeats per task × config
      --dry-run            Print the schedule and exit
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>  Per-run timeout in seconds
      --suite <SUITE>      Task suite (`graph` = with/without rtok MCP)
  -h, --help               Print help

$ rtok doctor --help
Inspect hooks, MCP servers and the proxy chain

Usage: rtok doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --instructions   Also run the instruction-file audit
      --json           JSON instead of the table
      --fix            Clean up broken hooks and duplicate hooks and MCP entries: a terminal gets a
                       checklist, a pipe the diff; --yes writes without asking
      --yes            With --fix: write the changes (a copy goes to `_backup/` first)
      --dry-run        With --fix --yes: print the diffs and write nothing
      --only <ONLY>    With --fix: limit it to these problems (repeatable; default: all of them)
                       [possible values: broken-hooks, duplicate-hooks, duplicate-mcp]
      --agent <HOST>   Check (and with --fix, repair) the hooks of one host only (an id of `rtok
                       agents list`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok info --help
Version, effective paths, disk usage, error count and proxy status

Usage: rtok info [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --json           JSON instead of the text lines
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents --help
Agent hosts (`rtok agents install|uninstall|list|info …`)

Usage: rtok agents [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  install    Install hooks, MCP server and proxy into a host
  uninstall  Take rtok back out of a host: hooks, MCP entry, proxy variable, plugin link [alias:
             remove]
  update     Bring what rtok installed up to date: in place where it can, reinstalled where not
  outdated   List hosts whose rtok plugin is older than this binary
  list       Every known app: kind and name, path and version, config files, rtok modules
  info       One host: the same block `agents list` prints, just for that app
  sessions   What is running in this project: host, provider, model, tokens, start, run time
  usage      Tokens and estimated cost per agent and month (or day), from the agents' logs or rtok
  junk       Junk and agent folders: `list` shows rtok's and every installed host's folders with
             sizes, `clear` removes rtok's own junk
  whoami     This session's own rtok agent id: `RTOK_AGENT_ID`, resolved through the store
  show       One agent by id prefix: host, model, ids, parent and sub-agents, cwd, activity, status
  status     Say what this agent (`RTOK_AGENT_ID`) is busy with: plain text, at most 120 chars
  send       Send a message to an agent: `send <id-prefix> <text|->` or `send --all-live <text|->`
  inbox      Read messages: your own inbox from `RTOK_AGENT_ID` (marks them read), or with an id
             that agent's queue (marks nothing)
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents install --help
Install hooks, MCP server and proxy into a host

Usage: rtok agents install [OPTIONS] <HOST>

Arguments:
  <HOST>  Host(s), comma-separated (`claude`, `cursor`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `zcode`, `kimi`,
          `copilot`, `aider`, `windsurf`, `zed`, `vscode`)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --dry-run        Print the planned edits and exit
      --remove         Remove rtok from the host (hooks, MCP, proxy, plugin link); prefer `rtok
                       agents uninstall <host>`
      --mode <MODE>    Enable prompt modes (`terse,yagni`)
      --yes            Confirm destructive `--replace`
      --replace        Remove legacy token hooks and retarget the proxy
      --mcp            Register `rtok mcp` in the host MCP map
      --proxy          Set `env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` to this proxy
      --cli            Only the CLI app (`cursor`/`opencode` have CLI and desktop; default is all)
      --desktop        Only the desktop app (`cursor`/`opencode` have CLI and desktop; default is
                       all)
      --all            All variants (the default when neither `--cli` nor `--desktop` is given)
      --no-restart     Skip closing/reopening a running desktop app around the write
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents uninstall --help
Take rtok back out of a host: hooks, MCP entry, proxy variable, plugin link

Usage: rtok agents uninstall [OPTIONS] <HOST>

Arguments:
  <HOST>  Host(s), comma-separated (`claude`, `cursor`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `zcode`, `kimi`,
          `copilot`, `aider`, `windsurf`, `zed`, `vscode`)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --dry-run        Print what would be removed and exit
      --no-restart     Skip closing/reopening a running desktop app around the write
      --yes            Also remove rtok entries you changed, without asking
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents update --help
Bring what rtok installed up to date: in place where it can, reinstalled where not

Usage: rtok agents update [OPTIONS] [HOST]

Arguments:
  [HOST]  Host(s), comma-separated; omitted = every host rtok is installed in

Options:
      --config <PATH>    User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --dry-run          Print the planned edits and exit
      --cli              Only the CLI app (default is all)
      --desktop          Only the desktop app (default is all)
      --all              All variants (the default when neither `--cli` nor `--desktop` is given)
      --no-restart       Skip closing/reopening a running desktop app around the write
      --force            Reinstall the plugin even when it is already at the available version
      --source <SOURCE>  Compare against this install source instead of the one on record [possible
                         values: github, local, marketplace]
      --check            List outdated plugins only (same output as `agents outdated`)
  -h, --help             Print help

$ rtok agents outdated --help
List hosts whose rtok plugin is older than this binary

Usage: rtok agents outdated [OPTIONS] [HOST]

Arguments:
  [HOST]  Host(s), comma-separated; omitted = every host in `agents list`

Options:
      --cli            Only the CLI app (default is all)
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --desktop        Only the desktop app (default is all)
      --all            All variants (the default when neither `--cli` nor `--desktop` is given)
      --json           JSON instead of the table
      --exit-code      Exit with code 10 when at least one plugin is outdated
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents list --help
Every known app: kind and name, path and version, config files, rtok modules

Usage: rtok agents list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --json           JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents info --help
One host: the same block `agents list` prints, just for that app

Whether that host's rtok MCP server answers: `rtok mcp ping <agent>`.

Usage: rtok agents info [OPTIONS] <HOST>

Arguments:
  <HOST>
          Host(s), comma-separated (`claude`, `cursor`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `zcode`, `kimi`,
          `copilot`, `aider`, `windsurf`, `zed`, `vscode`)

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)

      --json
          JSON instead of the table

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ rtok agents sessions --help
What is running in this project: host, provider, model, tokens, start, run time

Usage: rtok agents sessions [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  watch  Redraw the sessions table in place as sessions appear, end or spend
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --all            Also show sessions that have ended
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --json           JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents sessions watch --help
Redraw the sessions table in place as sessions appear, end or spend

Usage: rtok agents sessions watch [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --all            Also show sessions that have ended
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents usage --help
Tokens and estimated cost per agent and month (or day), from the agents' logs or rtok

Prices come from `[stats.prices]`; a model without one counts in the tokens and is left out of the
cost (`--unpriced` names those).

Usage: rtok agents usage [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)

      --source <SOURCE>
          Data source: `logs` (the agents' own session files, the default), `rtok` (what passed
          through rtok) or `both`

      --host <IDS>
          Only these hosts, comma-separated (`claude,codex`)

      --since <DATE|DUR>
          From a date (`2026-09-01`, whole days in `--tz`) or a duration back from now (`30d`)

      --until <DATE>
          Through this date, inclusive

      --daily
          Bottom table by day

      --monthly
          Bottom table by month (the default)

      --by <AGENT|MODEL>
          Middle table grouping: `agent` (the default) or `model`

      --tz <ZONE>
          IANA time zone for day and month boundaries (default: the system zone)

      --unpriced
          List the models without a price instead of the tables

      --json
          One JSON document

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ rtok agents junk --help
Junk and agent folders: `list` shows rtok's and every installed host's folders with sizes, `clear`
removes rtok's own junk

Usage: rtok agents junk [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list   Folders, junk kinds and sizes per agent, and the space `agents junk clear` would free
