$ rtok guard --help
Duplicate-call verdict (`rtok guard check` — pi / OpenCode plugin path)

Usage: rtok guard [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check  Print `{"allow":true}` or `{"allow":false,"reason":…}` (fail open: bad input allows)
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok guard check --help
Print `{"allow":true}` or `{"allow":false,"reason":…}` (fail open: bad input allows)

Usage: rtok guard check [OPTIONS] --tool <TOOL> --json <INPUT>

Options:
      --config <PATH>      User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --tool <TOOL>        Host tool name (`bash`, `Read`, …)
      --json <INPUT>       Tool arguments as JSON
      --session <SESSION>  Host session id (the cache is per session)
      --host <HOST>        Overlay `[hook] host`
  -h, --help               Print help

$ rtok demon --help
Keep `rtok proxy` (or `mcp` / `web`) running in the background

