$ rtok worktree --help
Git worktrees of this repository: owner, state and disk cost

Usage: rtok worktree [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     Create the worktree for a task: one location, one name, one locked owner; prints its path
  claim   Bind an existing worktree to an agent: rewrites its lock only when unlocked or already
          yours
  adopt   Bind the worktree you are in (made by a host's own tool) to your agent. A worktree in a
          pool its host evicts (Cursor, Codex, Windsurf, Devin) is claimed in the store only
  remove  Remove your own finished worktree: unlock, `git worktree remove`, delete the branch when
          merged, release the claim; refuses dirty, foreign-locked or current worktrees
  list    Every worktree and orphan with its owner, state, source and build-cache bytes
  gc      Remove merged, clean, idle worktrees with their branches; drop records of deleted ones
  clean   Delete idle tagged build caches (`CACHEDIR.TAG`) and keep the worktrees; dry run without
          `--yes`
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree list --help
Every worktree and orphan with its owner, state, source and build-cache bytes

Usage: rtok worktree list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --json           JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree gc --help
Remove merged, clean, idle worktrees with their branches; drop records of deleted ones

Usage: rtok worktree gc [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --yes            Apply; without it this is a dry run that changes nothing
      --owner <OWNER>  Open locks whose reason starts with this owner; every other lock is a hard
                       stop
      --idle <IDLE>    Keep worktrees modified within this window (`24h`, `7d`) [default: 24h]
      --json           JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree clean --help
Delete idle tagged build caches (`CACHEDIR.TAG`) and keep the worktrees; dry run without `--yes`

Usage: rtok worktree clean [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments:
  [PATHS]...  Only these worktrees; the one this command runs from is cleaned only when named

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --idle <IDLE>    Keep caches modified within this window (`24h`, `7d`) [default: 24h]
      --yes            Apply; without it this is a dry run that changes nothing
      --json           JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree add --help
Create the worktree for a task: one location, one name, one locked owner; prints its path

Usage: rtok worktree add [OPTIONS] <TASK> [SLUG]

Arguments:
  <TASK>  Task id, e.g. `t158`; directory `<repo>-<task>`, branch `<task>[-<slug>]`
  [SLUG]  Optional branch suffix

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --owner <OWNER>  Who holds it, as `<provider> / <model>`; written into the lock reason.
                       Defaults to `<host> / <model>` of the agent
      --agent <AGENT>  The rtok agent id (any unique prefix) to bind it to; defaults to
                       `RTOK_AGENT_ID`
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree claim --help
Bind an existing worktree to an agent: rewrites its lock only when unlocked or already yours

Usage: rtok worktree claim [OPTIONS] <PATH>

Arguments:
  <PATH>  The worktree

Options:
      --agent <AGENT>  The rtok agent id (any unique prefix); defaults to `RTOK_AGENT_ID`
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --owner <OWNER>  The owner an old lock names, as `<provider> / <model>`. Defaults to `<host> /
                       <model>` of the agent
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree adopt --help
Bind the worktree you are in (made by a host's own tool) to your agent. A worktree in a pool its
host evicts (Cursor, Codex, Windsurf, Devin) is claimed in the store only

Usage: rtok worktree adopt [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]  The worktree, or a directory inside it; defaults to the current directory

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --task <TASK>    The task id, when the lock and the branch do not name one (a detached HEAD)
      --agent <AGENT>  The rtok agent id (any unique prefix); defaults to `RTOK_AGENT_ID`
      --owner <OWNER>  The owner the lock names, as `<provider> / <model>`. Defaults to `<host> /
                       <model>` of the agent
      --json           Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok worktree remove --help
Remove your own finished worktree: unlock, `git worktree remove`, delete the branch when merged,
release the claim; refuses dirty, foreign-locked or current worktrees

Usage: rtok worktree remove [OPTIONS] <TARGET>

Arguments:
  <TARGET>  The worktree's path, or its task id (the lock's task or the branch `<task>[-<slug>]`)

Options:
      --agent <AGENT>  The rtok agent id (any unique prefix); defaults to `RTOK_AGENT_ID`
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --owner <OWNER>  The owner an old lock names, as `<provider> / <model>`. Defaults to `<host> /
                       <model>` of the agent
      --keep-branch    Remove an unmerged worktree too and keep its branch (a merged branch is kept
                       as well)
      --json           JSON instead of the text line
  -h, --help           Print help

```
